What is the language of the machine in Figure 4.2?











NoteCreating Non-deterministic Finite Automata Exercise




Take the DFA in Figure 2.2 and the DFA in Figure 2.4 and create an NFA that accepts strings that are accept by either machine. Creating an “OR” or union of two languages is very easy with NFAs. Free transitions are your friend here.
Create an NFA that begins with “101”. Allow your machine to let things fall off!
Create an NFA that ends with “101”. Hint, add a loop to your start state on “0,1”. This allows your machine to “guess” when it is at the end.

















